Bug 2052004 - Stop building unused libevent modules and add a moz.yaml. r=jld

https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2052004
Author: Ryan VanderMeulen [:RyanVM]

diff --git a/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/README.mozilla b/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/README.mozilla
--- a/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/README.mozilla
+++ b/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/README.mozilla
@@ -1,37 +1,33 @@
-This is a clean copy of libevent-2.1.13-stable with the following modifications.
+This is a clean copy of libevent, vendored via moz.yaml. Update it with:
 
-1. Add the following files:
+    ./mach vendor ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/moz.yaml
+
+That refreshes the upstream sources, preserves the Mozilla-maintained files listed below,
+and re-applies patches/prevent-use-of-evsig.patch (an intentional crash that prevents use
+of libevent's signal handling code; see bug 1616462). Only libevent's core event loop is
+compiled into libxul; see the source list in ipc/chromium/src/third_party/moz.build.
+
+The per-platform event2/event-config.h headers and evconfig-private.h are generated by hand,
+are not part of the upstream tree, and are preserved across a re-vendor (the "keep" list in
+moz.yaml):
 
 - android/event2/event-config.h
 - bsd/event2/event-config.h
 - linux/event2/event-config.h
 - mac/event2/event-config.h
 - solaris/event2/event-config.h
 - evconfig-private.h
 
-These files are taken from libevent-2.1.13-stable built on the development
-environment indicated by the first path component. You have to run
-"./configure" and "make" to get all of the pre-processing done. The
-event-config.h header can then be found in include/event2/ sub-directory and
-evconfig-private.h can be found in the root source directory.
-
-You then need to modify the EVENT__SIZEOF_* constants in the generated Linux,
-Android, and BSD headers to be appropriate for both 32-bit and 64-bit platforms.
-Mac doesn't need this since only 64-bit is supported. Use __LP64__ to
-distinguish the two cases. If you get something wrong, the CHECK_EVENT_SIZEOF
-static assertions in message_pump_libevent.cc will fail. If a new constant is
-added, also add a static assertion for it to message_pump_libevent.cc.
-
-You also need to modify the EVENT__HAVE_ARC4RANDOM and EVENT__HAVE_ARC4RANDOM_BUF
-constants in the generated Linux header to account for the results of the arc4random
-and arc4random_buf configure checks.
-
-2. Apply the following patch from ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/patches/:
+For a routine version bump, update the EVENT__*VERSION macros in each of these headers to
+match the new release, and fold in any EVENT__ macros that upstream added or removed.
 
-- "prevent-use-of-evsig.patch".  Prevents using (via intentional crash) any
-  of libevent's signal handling code; see bug 1616462.  This isn't strictly
-  required for functionality but it's a local patch we'd like to retain.
+When adding a new platform, or if an upstream config change affects these headers,
+regenerate the base header by running "./configure" and "make" on the target platform
+(event-config.h lands in include/event2/, evconfig-private.h in the root), then re-apply
+the Mozilla customizations these headers carry:
 
-Additionally, be careful to avoid clobbering changes to the various
-event-config.h files which have been customized over time to avoid
-various build bustages.
+- EVENT__SIZEOF_* are kept valid for both 32- and 64-bit builds using __LP64__ (Linux,
+  Android, and BSD; Mac is 64-bit only). The CHECK_EVENT_SIZEOF assertions in
+  message_pump_libevent.cc enforce this; a newly added constant needs a new assertion there.
+- EVENT__HAVE_ARC4RANDOM and EVENT__HAVE_ARC4RANDOM_BUF in the Linux header are guarded
+  rather than hardcoded (see bug 1782988).
diff --git a/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/moz.yaml b/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/moz.yaml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent/moz.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+schema: 1
+
+bugzilla:
+  product: Core
+  component: IPC
+
+origin:
+  name: libevent
+  description: Event notification library
+  url: https://libevent.org/
+  release: release-2.1.13-stable (2026-07-01T04:30:17-07:00).
+  revision: release-2.1.13-stable
+  license: BSD-3-Clause
+  license-file: LICENSE
+
+vendoring:
+  url: https://github.com/libevent/libevent
+  source-hosting: github
+  tracking: tag
+  vendor-directory: ipc/chromium/src/third_party/libevent
+
+  # Files added or maintained by Mozilla that must survive a re-vendor. The
+  # per-platform event2/event-config.h headers and evconfig-private.h are
+  # generated by hand (see README.mozilla) and are not part of the upstream tree.
+  keep:
+    - README.mozilla
+    - patches/
+    - evconfig-private.h
+    - android/
+    - bsd/
+    - linux/
+    - mac/
+    - solaris/
+
+  exclude:
+    - .clang-format
+    - .github/
+    - .gitignore
+    - .mailmap
+    - .uncrustify
+
+  patches:
+    - patches/prevent-use-of-evsig.patch
